        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/e274bd/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-08T15:22:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So I was watching Iron Man 3 this weekend, and &lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;MAYBE SPOILER ALERT?&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;Just in case you haven't seen it and are SUPER sensitive to the slightest of spoilers, seriously, stop reading&nbsp;[though I wouldn't personally classify this as a spoiler, since we've seen lots of evidence that Tony built lots of suits]&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>...when we saw a whole bunch of suits, I could have sworn one of them looked starkly (hehe) similar to the Bunker suit. It was only on-screen for a split second, and it was mostly head-and-shoulders, but the faceplate was so similar it made me laugh out loud (to the chagrin of my fellow moviegoers).</p><p>Please tell me I'm not the only one who noticed this.</p>",
